\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 The High Elvis
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 3 weeks to 2 months after Bombing
\f1 \
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f4\fs26 The unprecedented speed of their success necessitated the Elvi to organise into the Federation of Elvisian Enterprises. Being genetically identical, the Elvi readily adopted the concept of the equality amongst their number, however, self-organisation necessitated a hierarchical structure that did not sit well with the rank and file and many an argument broke out, each side able to hijack quotes of The Dawkins to support their claims. Selection of the Elvi leader, was fast-tracked, the entire process taking only days of campaigning and deal making and few rounds of voting until, obvious front-runner Elvis 457, was proclaimed leader. He immediately set off another lengthy set of arguments and enthusiastic karate fights when he proposed that the leader, that he, be referred to as \'91The King\'92. Every Elvis had dibs on the title of \'93The King\'94 and no individual would be permitted to appropriate it for themselves. They finally settled on \'93The High Elvis\'94, which was entirely accurate because Elvis 457 really loved his amphetamines. As did they all.\
\'93Praise be to the Dawkins.\'94 The first leader of the Elvi commenced his inaugural speech before a crowd of every Elvi in the Dominion. \'93As your first President, I am all shook up by the honour you bestow upon me. My hands are shaking and my knees are weak from the thought of a such a fool I, being gifted this pocket full of rainbows. I have a burning love for all of us in the ghetto. Suspicious minds may think I have taken this role to be the big boss man, but you are always on my mind and I love you so. As we travel along the long Jericho road, cross my heart and hope to die, we can make the morning and you\'92ll never walk alone. What we need is a little less conversation and a little more action so I washed my hands in muddy waters and they came out clean. It is no secret its a wonderful world and you\'92re the reason I\'92m living. If you give me all of your love, I\'92ll never stand in your way and there will be peace in the valley. I am pledging my love and let me be the one, but only the strong survive so please don\'92t stop loving me.\'94 He paused and the adoration of the Elvi spilled over into deafening applause and cheers. \
\'93The blessed mother carries the great one as we speak. As the arrival of the one-after-the-one approaches, brothers and sisters, we must prepare. We must also ready ourselves for the arrival of many thousands, tens of thousands of our overseas cousins at the World Elvis Convention later this year. For both of these wondrous events I propose changing the face of The Quarter. We will make our home a place where families can visit without fear of robbery, rape or murder.\'94 The vast mass of Elvi rose to their feet, clapping enthusiastically waving bright banners and whistling their new leader.\
\'93We must take our corner of the Primary Trade Dominion and transform it into a shining example of what can be achieved when the Elvi put their heads together. Look around you my fellow Elvi, the ground you stand upon is a rotting sludge of dirt, garbage and shit. We are all forced to live in this festering cesspool of filth and crime. We have been served up nothing but contempt, but we will rise above it all.\'94 A silent pause as the High Elvis looked over the crowd of adoring Elvi. \'93For the first time many decades we will revive communities, we will give people some pride and offer more than mere hope. The first proposal I have is for the beautification of the Pale.\'94 A cacophony of laughter erupted. \'93Yes, my Elvi. We are going to clean this place up, starting with old fashioned collecting of rubbish. Then we will scrub the footpaths, hose down the streets, shovel up the shit and make this place gleam. We will fix the drainage, water pipes and sewers.\'94 \
\'93You are joking.\'94 Elvis 3000 yelled out. \'93We are musicians, not street sweepers.\'94\
\'93We are much, much more. We are one hundred thousand strong and together in we can achieve anything. We will not need expensive machinery, our overwhelming numbers will effect change. How can anyone in The Pale ever get ahead when they live in the crushing poverty of this malevolent town? We cannot possibly evolve to our full potential if we are denied even the simplest of necessities. I submit that streets without clutter will give us all pride in our community and perhaps it will be the beginning of pride in ourselves. We will give ourselves the gift of dignity. It is a potent symbol of defiance. This is the way of The Dawkins.\'94 The High Elvis had no problems in co-opting The Dawkins for his own political gain.\
The crowd of Elvi erupted calling out in unison, \'93Praise be to the Dawkins.\'94\
\'93Indeed, praise be to the Dawkins. I have written a song for the inauguration today. We are the lucky few who have been granted the gift of life and we must use this precious gift to effect positive change. Who are we to complain if we do nothing to improve our situation? Who are we to complain about the inevitability of death? What of all the humans that could have been? The one\'92s that were never born? Most have Never Stirred.\'94 Elvis 457, the High Elvis, strummed his 12 string and effortlessly slipped into a heart-felt ballad for those who have never been.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

