\f3\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f4\fs26 The references, lifted directly from The Chronicles of The Dawkins, were unmistakable to the well-read gathering. The vast congestion of tearful Elvi clapped and cheered wildly, jumping and hugging each other at random, but the jubilation was soon replaced with panic. A group of five Elvi were lying flat, frothing at the mouth, in an apparent fit, each with ear-phones attached to a prehistoric music device. A small group gathered around them, one Elvis took the earphones from one of the Elvi, still jerking about on the ground and listened. His eyes widened and then threw the teeny speakers to the ground.\
\'93Gospel music!!\'94 He yelled and then vomited, stumbling as best he could for the nearest exit. Screams of panic filled the air as Elvi clamoured over each other in urgency and desperation, all heading in any direction away from the reviled tunes. The High Elvis rushed from the stage and stood before them in horror. They were not fitting, not like any epileptic he had ever seen. They were jerking about and talking some absolute gibberish as white foam spilled over their chins and the front of their jackets, running rivers of drool and bubbles between the rhinestones. Every so often, they would simultaneously break out into shouts of \'93Praise be to Jesus! The Lord and Saviour! Pledge now, pledge now.\'94\
\'93Blasphemy! Get these men out of here immediately.\'94 His inauguration reduced to farce, The High Elvis roared with anger . 
\f5\i What the hell has brought this on? 
\f4\i0 \'93Get them to a secure location and find out what they\'92ve been up to.\'94 \
Upon hearing the name of the ancient deity, Jesus, the manic Elvi ran away in disgust and fear, tugging at their hair and reefing out handfuls of jet black locks. They too, in their revulsion, called out, \'93Blasphemy\'94, \'93Apostate\'94 and \'93Unbeliever.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

